{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS6idW7t5Zky2z9YvyYM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the caching in `bot.py`. I couldn't check it against the real API (no key, SDK not installed), but a new offline test passes. The full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**The main cause was not the one in the colleague's note.** In `logs/usage.jsonl`, every `save_fact` happens in round 1 of a message, and the full-price miss comes in round 2 of that same message. `reply()` rebuilt the system prompt every round from the same athlete record that `save_fact` had just changed, so round 2 sent a different prompt.\n\n**What I changed:**\n1. **The system prompt is built once per message** and reused for every round. The model still sees the new fact in that message's tool call, and the fact appears in the prompt from the next message on.\n2. **The prompt is split into separately cached blocks:** instructions (never change), then the profile (date, name, sport, zones, goal, language), then one block per fact. Three cache markers (the limit is 4): after the instructions, after the profile, and on the last fact. `Language:` moved above the facts, because before it came after them and every new fact shifted it.\n3. **Facts only get added at the end.** So after a `save_fact`, the API finds the previous message's cached prompt and should only pay full price for the new fact, about 15 tokens instead of about 1,000.\n\n**Which parts of the note applied** (details in `ANSWER.md`): keeping the instructions separate and unchanging, keeping the tool filtering, loading all facts every time, and checking `usage`. \"Two markers is enough\" didn't apply as written:\n- It wouldn't fix the round-2 rebuild described above.\n- Anthropic only caches a prompt prefix of at least 1,024 tokens on Sonnet. From the log, tools plus instructions come to roughly 930 tokens, so the instructions-only marker is probably ignored for messages that only use the two core tools. The per-fact blocks work regardless, because each cached prefix there is the whole prompt.\n\n**Other files:** I added `tests/test_caching.py` (run `python3 tests/test_caching.py`) and updated the caching sentence in the README.\n\n**To confirm with real traffic:** trigger a `save_fact`, then send a follow-up within 5 minutes. Round 2 should show `cache_creation_input_tokens: 0`. The follow-up should read the old prompt from cache and only create about the size of the new fact.\n\n**Decision for you:** the instructions-only cache would start working if the plan and race tools were always sent (about 500 more tokens, read at 10% price). That would also stop the full re-caches when a message adds a tool group (the 1,305 and 1,334 in the log). `NOTES.md` says to leave tool filtering as it is, so I didn't change it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2208,"cache_read_input_tokens":41402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2208},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2401dd5-517c-4210-9fb0-9d2da94a3b73","uuid":"1b165a83-a498-4c07-a1de-d64aa37a1709","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:19:56.079Z","request_id":"req_011CgS6idC2XALK5K8sXtHmL"}
